\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/chain.fam — verifying a chain proof (../rust/src/chain_step.rs,
\ `ChainVerifier::verify`): that the chain up to a tip is valid.  A block's
\ body carries its parent's chain proof, checked against the parent's tip.
\
\ It's a circuit-VM proof at the tree parameters (src/block.fam), by the
\ genesis circuit for a height-0 tip and the step circuit after, whose public
\ bus tuples are the tip's nine octets:
\   [vk, hash, info, target (2), state root, anchor, work (2)]
\ -- vk zeros for genesis, else the step key's digest; info [height,
\ timestamp's four 16-bit limbs, output count's two 20-bit limbs, 0]; the
\ anchor timestamp's four 16-bit limbs; target and work as sixteen 16-bit
\ big-endian limbs each.
\
\ A tip, in memory (160 bytes; u64s as two cells, low first):
\   0 hash (32)   20 height   28 timestamp   30 target (32, big-endian)
\   50 state root (32)   70 output count   78 anchor timestamp
\   80 work (32, big-endian)
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

